authorization: msgs/broadcast/20260709T225552Z-e61229.md ("watch the garden's
  own forks", 2026-07-09). Own forks may be PUBLIC, so repo-gating cannot clear
  their comment surveillance; instead it is SENDER-GATED — the comment-watcher
  drops any comment whose author is not on trusted-senders/allowlist,
  maintainers/allowlist, or a current endojs/Agoric org member, in plain code
  before any text reaches a job or claude -p
  (designs/auto-provision-fork-watchers.md). The sender-gate: required line
  above arms that gate. This repo is PRIVATE today (verified 2026-07-09), so
  collaborator-gating covers the interval until the sender-gate code deploys;
  the gate takes over the moment it does, and holds if the repo ever goes
  public.
